What you want is a legend and the easiest way to do that is using melt
and setting the colour by variable which is what Takahashi and I
suggested. You can make your own legend but it's not something I have
done before.

I'm not sure why it didn't work though.

If you run:

#I didn't have "" around the variable name in my example last time
#that may have been the problem

datax2 <- melt(datax, id.vars="Distance")

d <- ggplot(datax, aes(x=Distance, y=value))

d + stat_smooth(aes(colour = variable), size = 2, alpha = 0.2)

What is the error that you get?

