Okay this finally working now. Here is what it turned out to be:

DF <- read.table("LightCurve.csv", header=TRUE, sep=",")
new.data<-melt(DF,id.vars="X",na.rm=FALSE, measure.vars=c("MMO.
645.","AKO.645."))
new.error<-melt(DF,id.vars="X",na.rm=FALSE,
measure.vars=c("Mrror","Arror"))

error <- new.error$value

G <- ggplot(new.data,aes(x=X,y=-value))+

geom_point(aes(shape = variable)) +
scale_shape(solid = FALSE) +
scale_x_continuous("JD - 2450000") +
scale_y_continuous("Magnitude Difference",breaks = c(-13, -12.5, -12,
-11.5, -11), label = c("13", "12.5", "12", "11.5", "11")) +
coord_cartesian()

Graph <- G + labs(shape = "Filter")

Graph2 <- Graph + geom_errorbar(aes(ymax = -value - error, ymin = -
value + error))

The errors without measurement curiosity was a mix up in excel.

Thanks for your help Brandon!

