An alternative is

install.packages("ggExtra", repos="http://R-Forge.R-project.org")
library(ggExtra)
align.plots(p1, p2)

>
> In the second plot: "opts(axis.title.x = theme_blank())" is not working,
> why?

It's getting confused by coord_flip. Putting the opts() call at the end works:

p2 = pb + geom_pointrange(size = 0.8) + geom_hline(yintercept=0.0,

colour = "green", size = 1, linetype = 2) + coord_flip()  +
ylab("Diferencia entre machos y hembras (ppm)") + theme_bw() +

scale_y_continuous(limits=c(0,3)) + opts(axis.title.x = theme_blank(),
legend.position = "none")

